  q(CLIN,'Which vein in the neck is often used to collect larger blood samples from cats and horses?','Jugular vein',['Cephalic vein','Lateral saphenous vein','Coccygeal vein in the tail'],'C','The jugular is large and easy to reach, so it gives a good sample quickly.',LAW),
  q(EMER,'Why should dogs and cats not be fed onions or garlic?','They can damage red blood cells and cause anemia',['They cause hair loss','They make teeth fall out','They are safe when cooked but cause skin rashes when eaten raw'],'D','Compounds in onions and garlic damage red blood cells, and cats are especially sensitive.',ARC),
  q(EMER,'Why must an owner never give a cat acetaminophen (Tylenol)?','Cats cannot break it down, and it damages red blood cells and the liver',['It makes cats sleepy','It is too bitter','It is safe for cats at the same weight-based dose given to small dogs'],'A','Even one tablet can be fatal to a cat, so human pain medicines should never be given without a vet.',ARC),
  q(EMER,'A dog’s toenail is cut too short and bleeds. What is a good first aid step?','Apply styptic powder or cornstarch with pressure',['Wrap the paw tightly with a rubber band','Let it bleed freely for several minutes to flush out bacteria','Soak it in hot water'],'B','Pressure with a clotting powder usually stops nail bleeding within a few minutes.',ARC),
  q(EMER,'A dog’s eye pops out of its socket after a fight. What should the owner do?','Keep the eye moist with saline or wet gauze and get to a vet at once',['Push it back in with fingers','Let it dry out','Gently push it back into place with clean, moistened fingers'],'C','Eye proptosis is an emergency, and the eye has a better chance of being saved if it stays moist.',ARC),
  q(EMER,'A puppy has chewed an electrical cord and is lying near it. What should be done first?','Turn off the power before touching the puppy',['Grab the puppy right away','Pour water on the cord','Pull the cord out of the puppy’s mouth with bare hands'],'D','Touching a pet that is still in contact with live current can shock the rescuer too.',ARC),
  q(EMER,'Blood soaks through a pressure bandage on a dog’s leg. What should the rescuer do?','Add more gauze on top and keep pressing',['Remove the soaked bandage','Rinse the wound with hot water','Stop pressing and let it clot'],'A','Removing the soaked layer pulls away the clot that is forming, so new layers are added on top.',ARC),
  q(SURG,'Which surgical scissors are fine and delicate, used for cutting and dissecting soft tissue?','Metzenbaum scissors',['Bandage scissors','Wire cutters','Mayo scissors, which are heavier and cut tough tissue'],'B','Metzenbaum scissors have long handles and short blades for precise work inside the body.',LAW),
  q(SURG,'Which type of suture breaks down inside the body over time?','Absorbable suture',['Nonabsorbable suture','Surgical staples','Stainless steel wire'],'C','Absorbable sutures are used under the skin so they do not need to be removed later.',LAW),
  q(SURG,'A male dog has one testicle that never descended into the scrotum. What is this condition?','Cryptorchidism',['Orchitis','Hernia','Prostatitis'],'D','Retained testicles have a higher cancer risk, so they are removed during neutering.',LAW),
  q(SURG,'What is it called when a surgical incision breaks open after surgery?','Dehiscence',['Seroma','Hematoma','Granulation'],'A','Licking, too much activity and infection can all cause dehiscence, which is why a cone and rest are used.',LAW),
  q(SURG,'Which approach is most commonly used for a routine spay in a dog?','A ventral midline incision',['An incision on the back','An incision through the flank on both sides','An incision through the chest wall'],'B','The ventral midline gives good access to both ovaries and the uterus through the linea alba.',LAW),
  q(SURG,'Which drug is commonly used as a local anesthetic for minor procedures in animals?','Lidocaine',['Ketamine','Propofol','Isoflurane, an inhaled general anesthetic'],'C','Lidocaine numbs a small area by blocking nerve signals, so the animal can stay awake.',LAW),
  q(ETH,'Which document lists the hazards and safe handling of each chemical used in a veterinary clinic?','Safety Data Sheet (SDS)',['Rabies certificate','Medical record','Client invoice'],'D','OSHA requires staff to have access to SDSs for every hazardous chemical in the workplace.',LAW),
  q(ETH,'Which federal law allows veterinarians to use approved drugs in ways not listed on the label, under certain rules?','AMDUCA',['HIPAA','The Animal Welfare Act','The Endangered Species Act'],'A','The Animal Medicinal Drug Use Clarification Act allows extra-label use within a valid vet-client-patient relationship.',LAW),
  q(ETH,'Where should used needles be placed in a veterinary clinic?','In a puncture-resistant sharps container',['In the regular trash','Recapped and left on the counter','In a paper bag'],'B','Sharps containers prevent needlestick injuries to staff and waste handlers.',LAW)
